    "terrainName": "cqb-village",
    "description": "What: On cqb-village, 'Blue Platoon' (Friend, 'Blue Squad 1-3', 4 men each, ~150 m south of OBJ) runs PlatoonAttack (AttackPosition, radius 20 round (125,161)) against NO enemy. Squads move for real; the check FAKES each phase report (Set, BuildingClear) over HTTP, so it tests the platoon's decisions. Judge: (1) one squad SquadDefends first as base of fire (fire at will) while the others wait; (2) its Set sends the others bounding, the assault to a flank point ~40 m off OBJ, the reserve behind; (3) the assault's Set makes it ClearBuilding OBJ and the base of fire only returns fire; (4) BuildingClear sends every squad to SquadDefend round OBJ, all Set ends the attack. Fail: a squad moves before the base of fire is Set, the assault never clears OBJ, or the attack never ends. Check: python3 scripts/utility-demo-check.py --launch pc-attack-dry"
  },
